CON-24: cap the snow pack's cold content at 0.007 x WSNOW x (Tbase - ATI)

SnowSolver::updateColdContent() copied legacy snow.c and limited the cold
content to wsnow * 0.007 / 12 * (tbase - ati), with wsnow and the cold
content both in ft, 12 times below the Reference Manual's
0.007 WSNOW (Tbase - ATI). Drop the /12. Same change as CON-24_swmm530.patch.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-24_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Snow.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Snow.cpp
index 5f27b5c..67cf6df 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Snow.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Snow.cpp
@@ -248,7 +248,8 @@ inline void updateColdContent(SnowSoA& soa, std::size_t ui, double temp,
     cc += soa.rnm * soa.dhm[ui] * (ati - temp) * dt * asc;
     cc = std::max(cc, 0.0);
     // maximum cold content based on assumed specific heat of snow
-    double ccMax = soa.wsnow[ui] * 0.007 / 12.0 * (soa.tbase[ui] - ati);
+    // (0.007 in. water equiv. per in. of snow per deg. F)
+    double ccMax = soa.wsnow[ui] * 0.007 * (soa.tbase[ui] - ati);
     cc = std::min(cc, ccMax);
     soa.coldc[ui] = cc;
     soa.ati[ui]   = ati;
